{
  "answer": "It is not possible to delete photos from your phone without deleting them from iCloud if you are using iCloud Photo Library, because iCloud syncs deletions across all devices. To keep photos in the cloud while removing them from your phone, you need to use a third-party cloud service like Dropbox or Amazon Photos, or disable iCloud photo syncing and manually transfer photos to a computer.",
  "citations": ["1", "4", "8", "9", "11", "12"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "You cannot delete photos from your phone without also deleting them from iCloud if iCloud Photo Library is enabled. To delete from your phone only, use a third-party cloud service (e.g., Google Photos, Dropbox) to back up photos, then delete from your phone. Alternatively, transfer photos to a computer first, then delete from your phone and turn off iCloud Photos.",
  "citations": ["3", "6", "11"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "It is not possible to delete photos from your phone without also deleting them from iCloud if you are using iCloud Photo Library, because iCloud syncs deletions. To keep photos in the cloud while removing them from your phone, use a third-party service like Dropbox or Amazon Photos to back up the photos, then delete them from your phone. Alternatively, you can enable 'Optimize iPhone Storage' in iCloud settings, which reduces photo file sizes on your phone while keeping full-resolution versions in iCloud, but this does not delete photos—it only optimizes storage.",
  "citations": ["3", "5", "6"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "If you have iCloud Photo Library enabled, deleting a photo on your phone will also delete it from iCloud. To delete photos from your phone without affecting iCloud, you must first disable iCloud Photos in Settings > [your name] > iCloud > Photos, or use a third-party backup service like Dropbox or Amazon Photos to store copies before deleting from the phone.",
  "citations": ["1", "2", "9"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

