{
  "answer": "Global iPhones (e.g., A1865 for iPhone X) support both GSM and CDMA networks, allowing them to work on a wider range of carriers worldwide. GSM-only iPhones (e.g., A1901 for iPhone X) work only on GSM networks, such as those used by AT&T and T-Mobile. GSM and CDMA are different cellular technologies; global phones combine compatibility with both.",
  "citations": ["1", "25", "22", "16", "23"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "A Global iPhone supports both GSM and CDMA networks, allowing it to work on multiple carriers worldwide, whereas a GSM iPhone only supports GSM networks and is limited to carriers like AT&T and T-Mobile.",
