{
  "answer": "You can see who is connected to your iPhone's personal hotspot by going to Settings > Cellular > Personal Hotspot, where you'll see a list of devices and the amount of data they've used. Alternatively, you can use a network scanner app like Net Analyzer on your iPhone to see connected devices. The status bar also turns blue and shows the number of connected devices.",
  "citations": ["lotte_technology_search_100k_c118280", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c111594", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c65689"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "You can't see a live list of currently connected devices, but you can view data usage per device by going to Settings > Cellular > Personal Hotspot. Alternatively, use a network scanner app like Net Analyzer to find connected devices by IP/MAC address. Note that devices signed into the same iCloud account may connect automatically.",
  "citations": ["lotte_technology_search_100k_c118280", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c104109", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c111594", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c87750"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "You can check who is connected to your iPhone's hotspot by going to **Settings > Cellular > Personal Hotspot** (under CELLULAR DATA), where you'll see a list of devices and their data usage. Alternatively, you can use a network scanner app like Net Analyzer to detect connected devices.",
