{
  "answer": "To delete photos from iCloud but keep them on your computer, you need to avoid using iCloud Photo Library as it syncs across all devices. Instead, first export or copy the photos from your Mac's Photos app to a separate folder on your computer. Then, delete them from the Photos library or iCloud. Alternatively, you can turn off iCloud Photo Library on your Mac (System Preferences > iCloud > Photos > deselect) to stop syncing, then delete photos from iCloud without affecting the local copies already on your Mac. Another option is to use a third-party cloud service like Dropbox for backup.",
