  "answer": "A CRL must be issued periodically because it is a signed, immutable snapshot of revocation information valid only for a specific time period. To ensure verifiers have up-to-date revocation data, new CRLs must be regularly published before the old ones expire, preventing reliance on stale information.",
  "citations": ["lotte_technology_search_100k_c547962", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c547965", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c549215"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

