{
  "answer": "To make an iTunes song your ringtone: 1. Choose a song in iTunes, right-click, select 'Get Info' > 'Options', set start and stop times (max 40 seconds). 2. Right-click the song, select 'Create AAC Version'. 3. Find the new file, rename its extension from .m4a to .m4r. 4. Delete the shortened version from iTunes (keep file). 5. Drag the .m4r file into iTunes Tones, or double-click to import. 6. Sync your iPhone: connect, select device, go to Tones, sync the ringtone. 7. On iPhone, go to Settings > Sounds > Ringtone, select your new tone. Alternatively, use GarageBand on iPhone/iPad to create a ringtone directly (chunk 4).",
  "citations": ["1", "2", "4", "7"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

{
  "answer": "To make an iTunes song your ringtone using a computer: 1) Select the song in iTunes, right-click > Get Info > Options, set start and stop times (max 30 seconds). 2) Right-click > Create AAC Version. 3) Right-click the new file > Show in Finder, rename extension from .m4a to .m4r. 4) Delete the short version from iTunes but keep the file, then drag the .m4r file back into iTunes (it will appear in Tones). 5) Sync your iPhone in iTunes, go to Tones, sync the ringtone, then set it on iPhone under Settings > Sounds > Ringtone. Alternatively, on iPhone, use GarageBand: import the song, long-press, share as Ringtone, then set under Settings > Sounds.",
  "citations": ["1", "2", "4"],
  "insufficient_context": false
}

