  "answer": "Physical cores are actual hardware components inside the CPU. Logical processors (or logical cores) are virtual cores created through hyperthreading technology, which allows a single physical core to execute multiple threads simultaneously. For example, a 4-core processor with hyperthreading can have 8 logical processors. The key difference is that physical cores are real hardware, while logical processors are abstractions that improve parallel processing.",
