{
  "answer": "You can transfer files from one Time Capsule to another using several methods. The most direct method via Finder: ensure both Time Capsules are on the same network and visible in Finder's Shared section (check Preferences > Shared > Connected servers). Mount both by double-clicking their names (default name \"Time Capsule xxxxxx\" and drive \"Data\"). Then drag your backup disk image (sparse bundle) from the old Time Capsule to the new one (chunks 11, 20, 36, 10, 14, 33). Alternatively, use AirPort Utility's \"archive disk\" function to copy the old Time Capsule to an external USB drive, then copy that to the new Time Capsule (chunks 5, 7, 12). For automated transfers, you can write a script using `mount_afp` and `unison` (chunks 15, 40). If using Time Machine, you can also set up a second backup to the cloud (chunks 3, 9). Note that transfers over network are slow (chunks 18, 19, 22).",
