  "answer": "The URG flag is a single bit in the TCP header that indicates the segment contains urgent data, while the urgent pointer is a 16-bit field that specifies the number of bytes from the start of the segment that are urgent. When the URG flag is set, the receiving station evaluates the urgent pointer to determine the urgent data.",
