  "answer": "Access lists (ACLs) are packet filters that can filter on higher-layer information like TCP/UDP ports and use wildcard masks for arbitrary address ranges, while prefix lists are route filters that match on prefixes and prefix lengths using ge/le keywords. ACLs have broader use (traffic filtering, QoS, NAT, security), whereas prefix lists are specifically designed for route filtering and redistribution, and are more expressive for that purpose.",
