  "answer": "The main difference is in how names are bound. 'import module' binds the module name to the module object, so you access attributes via module.attribute. 'from module import attribute' binds the attribute name directly, skipping the module lookup. Performance difference is negligible; both load the entire module. Use 'import module' for clarity and to avoid name collisions; use 'from module import' for readability when using a specific attribute many times.",
  "citations": ["lotte_technology_search_100k_c456809", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c456823", "lotte_technology_search_100k_c456825"],
