{
  "answer": "To connect an iPhone with a broken screen to a Mac, you can use a USB cable and QuickTime Player to view the screen. Connect the iPhone to the Mac, open QuickTime, select 'New Movie Recording', and choose your iPhone as the camera source. To control the iPhone or mirror the display, if the device was previously trusted on that computer, you can use AirPlay Screen Mirroring with server software like Reflector or AirServer on the Mac. If the device was never trusted and the screen is unresponsive, you may be able to use VoiceOver with a Bluetooth keyboard to tap 'Trust' when connecting via USB. Alternatively, a Lightning AV Adapter can sometimes display the screen without trusting the device.",
