{
  "answer": "GTK is the standard toolkit for GNOME, while Qt is used by KDE. From a user perspective, the main difference is cosmetic (looks). Licensing differs: GTK, as part of the GNU Project, uses LGPL allowing free use in proprietary software; Qt has a more restrictive licensing history, being freely available for non-profit but requiring a commercial license for some uses. Qt is a C++ framework, whereas GTK is a C toolkit. Additionally, different versions (GTK 2/3, Qt 3/4) are not backward compatible.",
